@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why a package exists for its exit-status types, how main turns them into proveo's exit code, and why the interface it was created for is never written
' covers: internal/backend/backend.go
' covers: internal/backend/backend_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go (main, exitWith, reraised, exitCode)
' covers: cmd/proveo/main_test.go (TestExitCodeIsTheAgentsOrTheStoppingSignals, TestAnInitACtrlCStoppedDiesOfSIGINT)
' covers: cmd/proveo/die_unix.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/die_windows.go
' covers: internal/sbx/run.go (RunExitCode)
' covers: internal/sbx/sbx_test.go (TestRunExitCodeTakesTheAgentsCodeSbxNamed, TestSaidErrorReadsSbxsOwnLastLine)
' covers: e2e/stream_palette_test.go (TestStreamPaletteE2E, TestNoProveoExitLineWhenOnlyStdinIsRedirected)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (agentEnd, sbxStatus, runResult)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/teardown_report_test.go (TestTheAgentsEndIsTheFirstResultLineOnlyWhenNothingElseSaidIt)
'   where a stop becomes Stopped .... _spec/internal/sbx/kit-lifecycle.puml
'   the transcript's outcome line .. _spec/internal/runlog/run-transcript.puml
'   the tail the code is read from . _spec/internal/agentio/agent-terminal-io.puml
'
' ── 2026-11-11 (R2): WHO SAYS THE EXIT ON SCREEN ───────────────────────────
' The operator, settled by P9 and the sbx overlap rule
' (_spec/_plans/output-readability.puml, F3): proveo prints no × when sbx
' printed its own error line; × only when sbx said nothing; never the agent's
' name when sbx may have failed before the agent started; none for a removal
' the operator chose at the Ctrl+C dialog.
'   sbx.SaidError(status, lines)  the tail's LAST line starts "error: " and
'                         is sbx's own: it names the agent's exit ("error:
'                         agent exited with code 3"), or sbx exited 1, the
'                         status that follows its own line ("error: stream
'                         I/O: context canceled")
'   sandbox.agentEnd      prints first under results: "× sbx run — exited
'                         with code N" for a bare *exec.ExitError sbx did not
'                         explain; "× <error>" for any other failure
'   sandbox.runResult     *exec.ExitError → ExitError{RunExitCode(...)}; a
'                         failure agentEnd printed, or any non-exit error of
'                         a removal the operator chose → backend.Reported
'   backend.Reported      main's exitCode returns 1 and main prints nothing,
'                         so no "× <err>" lands under a kept sandbox's "ide"
'                         block (the critique's item 8)
'   run.recordOutcome     ExitError goes to the LOG ONLY now
' A WRAPPED ExitError IS NOT sbx's EXIT. The Hermes Desktop hold returns
' "sbx setup ssh: %w"; it used to unwrap into ExitError{1}, "the agent exited
' with code 1". It is now a printed × and Reported (exit 1 either way).
' NO MODE IS BLIND TO sbx's LINE (R2 review fix, 2026-11-11). stdout on a
' terminal with stdin redirected has no pty proxy, so nothing fed the tail and
' the × repeated sbx's line. sbx writes its "error: …" line to STDERR (MEASURED
' on v0.50.0: `sbx exec <missing> 2>/dev/null` prints nothing; and with only
' stderr teed, the e2e below read "error: agent exited with code 3" and exited
' 3, where the binary without the tee printed "× sbx run — exited with code
' 1" and exited 1). agentio.Stdio
' now tees stderr on a terminal and leaves stdout the terminal itself
' (_spec/internal/agentio/agent-terminal-io.puml), so SaidError sees the line
' and RunExitCode reads the agent's code there too. The desktop hold never
' returns sbx's bare exit: its errors wrap sbx's captured output, so its × says
' what nothing else on screen said.
'   NOT CHOSEN: assume sbx spoke whenever the tail cannot see (a missing
'   verdict when sbx dies silent); keep the repeat as a recorded trade-off.
' Pinned by agentio TestStdioOnATerminalTeesStderrAloneSoSbxsErrorLineReachesTheTail
' and e2e TestNoProveoExitLineWhenOnlyStdinIsRedirected.
' THE LAST LINE IS sbx's ONLY WHEN THE STATUS AGREES (R2 review fix,
' 2026-11-11). In the pty and tee modes the tail mixes the agent's output with
' sbx's. An agent whose last line is its own "error: …", under an sbx that
' then dies without a line (a signal's -1, a Go panic's 2), read as "sbx
' said it": no ×, and RunExitCode found no code, so nothing on screen gave
' the exit. sbx exits 1 after its own error line (MEASURED: code 3 above;
' [Inference] from that one series, for its other errors), so SaidError takes
' the status: a line naming the agent's exit counts at any status; any other
' "error: " line counts only at status 1.
'   NOT CHOSEN: tee sbx's stderr apart in pty mode (sbx's stderr would stop
'   being a terminal, which changes how sbx draws); match sbx's known
'   messages (a list that drifts with every sbx release).
'   COST: [Unverified] an sbx that exits 1 with no line after the agent's own
'   "error: …" still reads as sbx's; no capture shows sbx doing that.
' AN OPERATOR-CHOSEN REMOVAL NEVER PRINTS × (R2 review fix, 2026-11-11).
' agentEnd checked "forced" inside the ExitError branch alone. When sbx
' exits 0 after the SIGTERM, exec.Cmd.Wait returns ctx.Err() (Go: a Cancel
' that succeeded makes a clean exit report the context), so the removal
' printed "× context canceled". agentEnd now returns no line for any forced
' result, and runResult returns it as backend.Reported: exit 1, silent.
' [Inference] Whether sbx v0.50 exits 0 on SIGTERM was not measured.
' Pinned by TestSaidErrorReadsSbxsOwnLastLine (the status rows) and the
' "sbx exited 0" row of TestTheAgentsEndIsTheFirstResultLineOnlyWhenNothingElseSaidIt.
' The e2e TestNoProveoExitLineWhenOnlyStdinIsRedirected asserts PROVEO_EXIT=3.
' MOVED: e2e/stream_palette_test.go no longer reads proveo's bold × (sbx's
' "error: agent exited with code 3" is the verdict there); the bold head of a
' × line is pinned by internal/ui TestOnlyTheSeverityHeadKeepsTheTerminalColour.
' Pinned by TestTheAgentsEndIsTheFirstResultLineOnlyWhenNothingElseSaidIt,
' TestSaidErrorReadsSbxsOwnLastLine, and the Reported row of
' TestExitCodeIsTheAgentsOrTheStoppingSignals.
'
' ── 2026-10-20: sbx EXITS 1 AND NAMES THE AGENT'S CODE ─────────────────────
' MEASURED by e2e/stream_palette_test.go (fake agent exits 3): the screen read
' `error: agent exited with code 3` from sbx, then proveo's own
' `× the agent exited with code 1` and PROVEO_EXIT=1. Run passed `sbx run`'s
' process status through (ExitError{ee.ExitCode()}), and that status was 1.
' [Inference] The newer sbx prints the agent's code, then exits 1 itself.
' FIX: sbx.RunExitCode(status, tail.Lines()) — pure, internal/sbx/run.go:
'   status ≠ 1                          → status (137, 0, a signal's -1)
'   status = 1, a line matches
'   `agent exited with code (\d+)`      → the LAST match, when it is non-zero
'   last match names 0, or none matches → 1 (sbx's own failure stays 1)
' "-1" never matches (\d+), so sbx's "code -1" for a killed agent stays 1.
' Run applies it where it builds ExitError, on BOTH paths that feed the tail:
' the pty proxy's OutTap (headed, filtered) and the MultiWriter tee
' (streamed, non-TTY). A TTY run with the filter off and no stdin trace hands
' sbx the terminal directly, so its tail is empty and the status stays sbx's.
' (Since R2's review the stderr tee feeds that tail too; see above.)
' Pinned by TestRunExitCodeTakesTheAgentsCodeSbxNamed (sbx_test.go): named,
' no line, code 0, last line wins, last match in a line wins, negative, and
' status pass-through.
'
' ── 2026-11-11 (R3 review): INIT DIES OF THE SIGINT IT WAS HANDED ──────────
' A Ctrl+C in a program `proveo init` handed the terminal to (sbx setup, sbx
' login, gh auth login, an installer) reaches that program; init prints its
' blocks and "⚠ init — stopped at <row>", then returns reraised{Stopped
' {SIGINT}}. exitWith calls dieOf: signal.Reset, kill(self, SIGINT), so the
' shell that waits on init sees a process SIGINT ended. bash's
' wait-and-cooperative-exit then stops that shell too: install.sh's `proveo
' init </dev/tty || init_incomplete` no longer prints init_incomplete and the
' post-install message after a Ctrl+C. Exit 130 alone read as a child that
' handled the Ctrl+C, and the caller went on. MEASURED (macOS /bin/sh, bash
' 3.2.57): a child that exits 130 lets `sh -c "child; echo went on"` print
' "went on"; a child SIGINT ends stops it. When SIGINT is ignored dieOf
' returns after 1s and exitWith exits 130. Windows has no signal to re-raise:
' exit 130 there. A run's Stopped keeps its plain 128+signal exit: its
' teardown e2e reads the status through a shell (NOT CHOSEN: re-raise every
' Stopped). Pinned by TestAnInitACtrlCStoppedDiesOfSIGINT (a helper process
' that must die of SIGINT) and e2e TestInitCtrlCInSbxsWizardEndsOnWhereItStopped
' (a wrapper shell like install.sh's stops; the outer one, trapping INT, reads
' 130).
'
' ── 2026-11-10: Stopped ALSO NAMES A TEARDOWN THE OPERATOR LEFT ────────────
' The Executor, on Ctrl+C during teardown: "Say once, leave on two", and on
' SIGTERM or SIGHUP there: "Finish the step, then leave".
' Run now returns Stopped{Signal} when a signal made TEARDOWN leave part of
' its plan undone, whatever the agent's own result was:
'   Stopped{SIGINT}.Code()  130   Error() "stopped by SIGINT"
'   SIGTERM 143 and SIGHUP 129, as below
' A signal that arrives in the last step leaves nothing undone; the run's own
' result stands. Why and how: _spec/internal/backend/teardown.puml (T4).
' Pinned by TestAStopExitsWith128PlusTheSignal (the SIGINT row) and
' TestExitCodeIsTheAgentsOrTheStoppingSignals ("a teardown the operator left").
'
' ── 2026-10-17: A SECOND TYPE, Stopped ─────────────────────────────────────
' The user, on a stopped run's exit status: "Exit 128+sig, 'stopped'
' (Recommended)". MEASURED, internal/backend/backend.go:
'   type Stopped struct{ Signal syscall.Signal }
'   Error() "stopped by SIGTERM" | "stopped by SIGHUP" | "stopped by signal N"
'   Code()  128 + signal → 143 for SIGTERM, 129 for SIGHUP
' internal/backend/sandbox Run returns Stopped when a forwarded SIGTERM/SIGHUP
' ended the run and the operator had not chosen Ctrl+C remove; teardown runs as
' on a normal exit. cmd/proveo main's exitCode(err) recovers ExitError → Code
' and Stopped → Code() through errors.As, and main calls os.Exit with it,
' printing nothing; any other error prints and exits 1. So a shell, CI step or
' the scheduler's `echo $? > <run>.exit` reads 143 for a stop, the status a
' shell reports for a process SIGTERM ended. A stop is neither success (0) nor
' proveo's own failure (1).
' Pinned by TestAStopExitsWith128PlusTheSignal (backend_test.go, through a %w
' wrap) and TestExitCodeIsTheAgentsOrTheStoppingSignals (main_test.go).
' COVERAGE CHOICE: cmd/proveo/main.go and main_test.go are covered here because
' main and exitCode turn the command's error into proveo's process status; a
' change there must flag this spec even though both files mostly hold unrelated
' commands. Expect drift reports from those unrelated edits too.
' The package-placement argument below applies to Stopped as it does to
' ExitError: internal/backend/sandbox builds it and cmd/proveo reads it.
' internal/run's recordOutcome only prints it (%v), through its default branch.
'
' ── 2026-10-16: ONE BACKEND LEFT ───────────────────────────────────────────
' internal/backend/dockeregress is DELETED with the docker+egress backend
' ("Retire Docker egress"); internal/backend/sandbox is the only consumer of
' ExitError besides cmd/proveo, and run.selectBackend became launchSandbox. The
' dependency-direction argument below weakens with one backend: placing
' ExitError inside internal/backend/sandbox no longer forces a sibling import.
' DECIDED 2026-10-18 (repo-simplification.puml N16, option 2): the user's
' "Apply N16" took the [rec], "Keep the package as the home of run errors;
' nothing else to do". No source changed. MEASURED: three packages import it —
' internal/backend/sandbox builds both types, internal/run matches ExitError in
' recordOutcome, and cmd/proveo maps both to a status in exitCode.
' Everything below that names dockeregress or "both backends" is HISTORY.
'
' ── NO INTERFACE, AND THAT IS THE FINISHED STATE ───────────────────────────
' (Until 2026-10-17 the package held ONE type, ExitError; Stopped is the second.)
' The package was created during the cmd/proveo decomposition to hold what the
' two backends share, with a Plan(RunSpec)/Execute(Plan) interface promised once
' RunSpec existed. RunSpec now exists. THE INTERFACE IS STILL NOT WRITTEN, and
' the promise is withdrawn rather than left standing.
'
' Nothing consumes the backends polymorphically. run.selectBackend branches on
' which one won and calls each by name, because their shapes genuinely differ:
' sandbox.Run takes an Input and runs, while dockeregress splits into Assemble
' then Exec so the caller can start a review gate BETWEEN the two. An interface
' over two divergent implementers with no caller holding one describes nothing —
' it guesses a shape, which is the abstraction Go's own advice says to declare at
' the CONSUMER once a consumer exists.
'
' ── WHY THE PACKAGE STAYS ANYWAY ───────────────────────────────────────────
' Not for abstraction — for dependency direction. ExitError is needed by
' cmd/proveo and by BOTH backends. Put it in either backend and the other has to
' import its sibling; put it in cmd/proveo and internal/ imports cmd/. A leaf
' package is the only placement that leaves the graph acyclic.
'
' ── WHAT THE TYPE ACTUALLY GUARDS ──────────────────────────────────────────
' proveo's exit status must be the AGENT's, not proveo's own. A backend returns
' ExitError from deep inside a run and main recovers it with errors.As, so a CI
' step sees what the agent decided. The value must therefore survive wrapping:
' TestExitErrorSurvivesWrapping pins that, because a type that stopped matching
' through a %w chain would silently turn every agent failure into exit 1 and no
' test of the happy path would notice.
title internal/backend — a package for dependency direction, not abstraction

participant "sandbox" as SBX <<cloud>>
participant "backend.ExitError" as EE <<data>>
participant "backend.Stopped" as ST <<data>>
participant "cmd/proveo main\nexitCode" as MAIN <<app>>

SBX ARROW_ERROR EE : agent exited 137
SBX ARROW_ERROR EE : sbx exits 1 after "agent exited with code N"\n→ N via sbx.RunExitCode(1, tail)
EE ARROW_MAIN MAIN : errors.As through the wrap chain
MAIN ARROW_MAIN MAIN : os.Exit(code) — the AGENT's code
SBX ARROW_ERROR ST : forwarded SIGTERM/SIGHUP,\nnot the Ctrl+C remove path
ST ARROW_MAIN MAIN : errors.As through the wrap chain
MAIN ARROW_MAIN MAIN : os.Exit(128+signal) — 143 / 129

note over EE
  **No Plan/Execute interface.** One implementer
  since 2026-10-16 (dockeregress deleted), and no
  caller that holds one. Declared at the consumer,
  if a consumer ever appears.
end note

note over ST
  **A stop exits 128+signal, not 0 or 1.**
  143 for SIGTERM, 129 for SIGHUP: what a shell
  reports for a process the signal ended. main
  prints nothing for it, as for ExitError.
end note
@enduml
